op working on the  issues it just means you you stop  campaigning so aggressively on that  because it turns a lot of those rural  folks off number two  you figure out how to better talk to  farmers and agricultural  employers and workers and number three  you tweak the economic message to  not be so union heavy but more about  understanding  the plight of a lot of these  economically ravaged areas  where whether the one employer is  unionized or not and i support the  unionization  that's not a path to fixing or dealing  with  the way that the area has been ravaged  big picture  overwhelmingly by the republican sort of  supply side policies that came out of  the 1980s those would be my three kind  of bits of advice  for democrats to better appeal to rural  voters and the truth is that appealing  to rural voters  in california versus mississippi  are certainly two different things and  and the midwest as a third one  those are my initial thoughts let me  know what you think we have a fantastic  bonus show for you today  get instant access by becoming a member  at joinpakman.com see you then one of  our sponsors is privacy.com they're  giving you five dollars when you sign up  for their completely  free service at privacy.com  pacman i've been using privacy for a  little over a year now you've heard me  talk about it before  it's a lifesaver and here's how it works  takes just a couple of minutes to set up  anytime you buy something online or on  the phone  instead of actually using your real  credit card number  the privacy app and the browser plug-in  let you give each company  a randomized virtual credit card number  that you create out of thin air  it'll even auto fill the card number  with one click and the payment  is taken out of your checking account  without the merchant ever knowing your  real information so this allows you to  keep  your banking information secure but also  to take control of your finances you can  create  up to 12 of these virtual credit c